%N A135140 Numbers k such that k and k^2 do not contain successive identical digits.
%C A135140 Infinite since 27*(100^m - 1)/99 is a term iff m mod 11 != 3 and 72*(100^m - 1)/99 is a term iff m mod 11 is not in {2,6,7}. - _Lien-Hung Su_, Oct 30 2026
%H A135140 G. C. Greubel, <a href="/A135140/b135140.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A135140 Lien-Hung Su, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23224633">Adjacent-Digit Distinct Squares from Repeated 27 and 72 Blocks</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%t A135140 Select[Range[0,150],Count[Differences[IntegerDigits[#]],0] == Count[ Differences[IntegerDigits[#^2]],0]==0&] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Mar 14 2012 *)
